//? Title: Medical volumes:genuine CT cubes and visible tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original NoduleMNIST3D cubes feed a complete custom three-stage residual CNN. Explicit fitting-only normalization,all48Adam updates,volumetric previews and every held-out record expose the limited dataset-label result.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/medical_volume_classification.cpp`.

> The method

Preserve official released-array boundaries and original byte intensities,compute fitting-only moments with tensors,and show the full residual3Doptimizer loop. Restore20learned tensors and two moments for intensity-only inference,then compare every held-out record and depth control with a fixed memory reference.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/medical_volume_classification_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/medical_volume_classification_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/medical_volume_classification_concept.tikz > build/medical_volume_classification_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/medical_volume_classification_concept.svg build/medical_volume_classification_concept.dvi > build/medical_volume_classification_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
