> Genuine released CT cubes and official array boundaries

Use corrected NoduleMNIST3D v2.1,29299364bytes,SHA256
5dc6f82bdb2b91f300263522aab82f7c034d0b264692f6d5f4c70179ad27f76b,
MD58755a7e9e05a4d9ce80a24c3e7a256f3. Released28x28x28uint8cubes derive
from LIDC-IDRI lung nodules. The dataset calls source0benign(ratings1/2),
source1malignant(ratings4/5),and excludes rating3. These are released dataset
labels,not diagnoses made or validated by this teaching model.

Retain the first32fit/8validation/32test distinct records per class in source
row order:64/16/64balanced cubes. Official array sizes1158/165/310 give exact
source-ID offsets0/1158/1323;selected IDs remain disjoint. Skip byte-identical
selected cubes across all pools. Original archive bytes and every selected
source row remain available. Patient independence cannot be verified from
these released row IDs. This small subset is not clinical validation or a full benchmark.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("medical", (cache / "medical_volume").string());
}
```
