> Verification and limits

Five native tests cover all646independent signed residual/projection/bias/input
finite differences,all20actual learned gradients/stage inventories,every3161088
selected source voxel/label/ID,every fitting moment/block feature and reference
prediction,and independent intensity-only restoration/invalid contracts.
Public examples compile/run;the original three-epoch workflow passes.
The selected CNN accuracy60.94%is below block1NN64.06%;its source1recall.25
means24of32source1records are missed. This balanced144record teaching subset
and unverified patient identity support no full-dataset or clinical claim.

> Conclusion

The tensor model and independent numerical/source-data checks pass,but held-out dataset-label accuracy remains below the fixed block1NNreference. Complete errors and preserved source semantics support a reproducible teaching example without clinical or full-benchmark claims.

> References

- [Yang et al.(2023),MedMNIST v2:A large-scale lightweight benchmark for2Dand3Dbiomedical image classification](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01721-8).
- [Corrected official NoduleMNIST3D v2.1 archive](https://zenodo.org/records/6496656).
- [Official original dataset-label and split description](https://github.com/MedMNIST/MedMNIST/blob/main/medmnist/info.py).
